### Modifications

Changes made to the absorbed code are marked in-source with `cash (Dnn)`
comments referencing the decision in [spec.md](spec.md). As of absorption:

- `brush-parser`: `case` constructs are consumed whole inside command
  substitution, in both the tokenizer and the word parser (§9.1)
- `brush-core`: CRLF line terminators in command substitution (D20), UTF-8 BOM
  stripping when sourcing scripts (D41), the path model in `set_working_dir`
  and `absolute_path` (D3/D10), and a dependency on `cash-win32`
- `brush-builtins`: CRLF line terminators in `read` (D20)
- Removed: `brush` (a binstall alias crate), `brush-experimental-builtins`,
  `fuzz`, `benchmarks`, upstream documentation, CI and release tooling
